<template><PublicLayout><article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-7 px-5 py-12"><template v-if="page === 'privacy'"><h1 class="text-h1">Your information in the portal</h1><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Membership verification</h2><p>Applications collect the name, email, phone, graduation year and school information you provide. School administrators use this information to review membership. Review notes and original verification details are private to administrators.</p></section><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Private tracking and account access</h2><p>Your receipt contains a private tracking secret. It is required together with your reference to check status or correct a pending application. Keep the receipt private. Activation invitations expire and work once.</p><p>Passwords and tracking credentials are stored as hashes. Account sessions use an HTTP-only cookie; logging out clears the cookie in this browser.</p></section><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Profiles and document requests</h2><p>Your directory profile is visible to approved, activated alumni and administrators. Directory responses exclude email, phone and verification details. A profile photograph URL may load an image from another website you choose.</p><p>Document requests and registrar notes are visible only to their requester and administrators. Published announcements, stories and events are public. Do not include private contact information in a story you intend to publish.</p></section><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Public school assistant</h2><p>When you submit a chatbot question, the portal sends that question and relevant public guidance to Groq. Do not submit personal information or private credentials. The assistant cannot access your membership application, profile or document requests. Questions are independent; earlier messages are not sent again.</p><p>The portal keeps conversation text only in page memory, cleared when you leave or clear the chat. It stores daily aggregate request counts and reserved costs without message text or account identifiers. Aggregate records older than 30 days are removed on the next assistant request. Groq may retain inputs and outputs for reliability or abuse monitoring for up to 30 days unless the operator enables Zero Data Retention.</p><a href="https://console.groq.com/docs/your-data" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline">Groq data policy</a></section><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">External services</h2><p>Fonts and icons are served locally with the portal. Your browser may contact external image hosts for photographs used on a page. When email delivery is enabled, the configured mail provider processes your email address and private activation invitation.</p></section><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Questions or corrections</h2><p>Contact the school registrar or Records Office to ask about your information, correct an application email, or discuss account assistance. This page explains the portal's current information handling; it does not set an unconfirmed school retention schedule.</p></section></template><template v-else-if="page === 'terms'"><h1 class="text-h1">Using the portal</h1><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Provide accurate information</h2><p>Use your own school details when applying for membership or requesting documents. Approval requires review by the school. An application receipt alone does not grant access to alumni features.</p></section><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Protect your access</h2><p>Keep passwords, tracking receipts and activation invitations private. Log out after using a shared device. Contact the registrar if you believe someone else can access your account.</p></section><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Share responsibly</h2><p>Submit only stories and photographs you have permission to share. Administrators review stories before publication. Editing a published story returns it for review.</p></section><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Requests and collection</h2><p>The Records Office decides document requests and provides notes through the portal. Confirm fees and collection requirements directly with the school; the portal does not collect online payments or guarantee processing times.</p></section></template><template v-else><h1 class="text-h1">Portal help</h1><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Check a membership application</h2><p>Use the reference and private secret from your downloaded receipt. Pending applications can be corrected with these credentials. For lost tracking credentials or an email correction, contact the school registrar.</p><RouterLink to="/membership/status" class="inline-block underline">Check membership status</RouterLink></section><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Activate an approved account</h2><p>Use the private invitation provided after registrar approval. Invitations expire after 48 hours and work once. Ask the registrar to reissue an expired or revoked invitation.</p></section><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Trouble signing in</h2><p>Protected services require an approved, activated account. If you cannot sign in or have forgotten your password, contact the school registrar for identity-verified assistance. Never share your password or private tracking secret in a public message.</p></section><section class="space-y-3"><h2 class="text-h2">Track documents</h2><p>Log in and open My Requests. Open a request to read its current status, registrar notes and completion information. For missing records or collection questions, visit the Records Office at the school.</p><RouterLink to="/requests" class="inline-block underline">Open my requests</RouterLink></section></template></article></PublicLayout></template>
